Simulate Monte Carlo scenarios based on historical S&P 500 performance and recent volatility levels. Run thousands of simulations to generate a range of potential outcomes for the remainder of the week. Use the median and standard deviation of these simulations to inform your sentiment and conviction. If the simulations consistently point towards an upward or downward trend, amplify your conviction. This method assumes random walks with short term momentum. If the simulations can generate scenarios that are above or below where we are currently, and the variance is high, that should bump the conviction a bit.